is an edge. The goal is to minimize the number of edges in a graph with 23 vertices where each vertex has a degree of at least 1 (i.e., each person shakes hands with at least one other person).\n\nThe minimum number of edges in a graph where each vertex has a degree of at least 1 is achieved by having a spanning tree. A spanning tree of a graph is a subgraph that is a tree and includes all the vertices of the original graph. In a tree with \\( n \\) vertices, there are exactly \\( n-1 \\) edges.\n\nHere, \\( n = 23 \\), so the minimum number of edges (handshakes) is:\n\\[\n23 - 1 = 22\n\\]\n\nTo verify, consider a tree with 23 vertices. In a tree, each vertex is connected to at least one other vertex, and the number of edges is exactly one less than the number of vertices. Therefore, the minimum number of handshakes is indeed 22.\n\nThus, the minimum possible number of handshakes is \\(\\boxed{22}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{22}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"counting_and_probability:466"}
